<title>BRAZIL: American, TAM in partnership.</title>
<headline>American, TAM in partnership.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Airlines and Brazilian airline TAM said they have struck a deal to form a code-sharing partnership that will allow passengers to swap tickets, reservations and other services between the carriers.</p>
<p>The companies, in a joint statement, said the partnership will cost $10 million to implement and also will allow both airlines to issue TAM and American Airlines tickets and recognize each others frequent-flier mileage programs.</p>
<p>The code-sharing agreement was to be signed at a ceremony this morning and the partnership will take effect August 1.</p>
</text>
